# Library packages

Edit the smallest package that owns the behavior. Shared protocol starts in `core`, then `server` and `react` — no duplicate route strings or schemas. Upload keys are server-owned (no client `key` on upload / multipart init).

Auth stays in consumer guards. No ORM in `server`. Feature plugins (e.g. `db()`) live in their own package; merge once in `dimahS3()`. Throw `APIError` and let the router serialize. Do not wrap trivial S3 APIs (`s3.put` and `GET /file` are the exceptions).

**When adding a package or moving behavior across packages, Read** [docs/agents/architecture.md](docs/agents/architecture.md).

**When changing published API, protocol, endpoints, plugins, or hooks, Read** [docs/agents/packages.md](docs/agents/packages.md).

For a local fix, match the surrounding code.
